# ─── Mobile app environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env` and adjust. Only EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars are visible to app code.
#
# You usually do NOT need to set anything here for local development:
# when you run `npx expo start`, the app auto-detects your machine's LAN IP
# from the Expo dev server and talks to http://<that-ip>:8080/api.
#
# Set this only when you need to override that, e.g. to point a local build at
# the deployed backend, or when running on a device on a different network.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.100.38:8080/api
#
# Production (Render) example — the trailing /api is optional, it is added
# automatically if missing:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://gb-cattle-backend.onrender.com/api
